0. Definitions
   "Software" means this repository and its contents.
   "You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights.
   "Public Instance" means making the Software available so that people beyond
   a private personal group can create accounts, join, or discover the service
   (including a public registration page or advertised community).
   "Use the code" means copying or incorporating any substantial portion of
   the Software into other software or services, or redistributing the
   Software outside the limited hosting-service fork described in section 1(d).
   Platform forks used only to view, study, or contribute under the CLA are
   not "Use the code" by themselves.

1. Limited grant
   Provided you comply with these terms, the copyright holder grants you a
   non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable copyright license to:
   (a) view and study the Software;
   (b) compile and run one private instance for personal, non-commercial use
       that is not a Public Instance (invite-only household/friends use is
       allowed; advertised or general-public use is not);
   (c) make private modifications solely to run that instance;
   (d) fork the repository using functionality provided by the repository
       hosting service solely for viewing, studying, or contributing to
       VoxNexus under the CLA. Such a fork does not grant permission to
       operate a Public Instance, redistribute, commercialize, or
       incorporate the Software into another project.
   A limited patent license is granted only for the same permitted purposes
   and only for claims the copyright holder can license that you would
   infringe by exercising this grant.

2. Prohibited without a separate written license from the copyright holder
   (a) any commercial use, including use by or for a for-profit organization
